text:
**Review Result**

Score: **6.5/10**. The code is small, readable, and has a solid happy-path test suite, but I would not approve it as-is because several accounting correctness bugs can silently produce wrong usage/state data.

Tests: `pytest -q` passes, 61 passed. Only warning was pytest cache creation in this environment.

Estimated rewrite/significant-change size: **150 lines**, including tests. Most of that is upsert/state ordering, timestamp normalization, validation, DB open modes/permissions, and indexes.

Bottom line: **No, I would not approve this PR as-is.**

```json
{
  "score": 6.5,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "70-101",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Same-rank terminal records update unconditionally, so an older FAILED/TIMEOUT/etc. snapshot can overwrite a newer terminal record."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "74-80",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "The unchanged check only compares state, end, and elapsed_sec, so corrected user/partition/CPU/GPU/exit_code data is silently ignored."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "31-41",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Unknown Slurm states are treated as terminal, causing in-progress states like CONFIGURING, REQUEUED, or RESIZING to interact incorrectly with stale-skip logic."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "14, 58-69, 113-121, 135-148",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Timestamps are stored and compared as raw text, which gives incorrect ordering/filtering when timezone offsets or mixed timestamp forms are present."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "148-163",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Negative AllocCPUS and negative gres/gpu values are accepted, allowing negative CPU/GPU-hour reports."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "152-164",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Rows with submit, start, and end all missing are accepted but disappear from all time-filtered reports and top-user windows."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "52-58",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Read-only report commands use the same connect path as ingest, so a typo or missing DB path silently creates an empty database."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "55-56",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "The default database directory and file are created with process umask defaults, which can expose job/user accounting data on shared systems."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "13-27",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "The schema has no indexes for reference-time, user, partition, or state report queries, so reports become full-table scans at Slurm accounting scale."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 150,
  "approve": false
}
